{
  "comment": [
    "Cross-language conformance vectors for DNS name validation.",
    "Consumed by Tests/MacDNSTests/DomainNameConformanceTests.swift and by the",
    "conformance module in rust-resolver/crates/macdns-resolver/src/domain_name.rs.",
    "owners: DNSPolicySemanticPolicy.canonicalName / domain_name::canonicalize.",
    "owners.role: override (override owner) or forwardZone (forward-zone apex).",
    "targets: DNSPolicySemanticPolicy.targetNameRejection / hickory Name::from_str.",
    "forwardTargets: DNSResolverAddressParser / zones::validate_forward_target.",
    "Contract both suites assert: whenever swift.accept is true, rust.accept must",
    "be true and the canonical forms must be identical. Swift is allowed to be",
    "stricter — a name the App refuses can never reach state.json — but a name the",
    "App accepts and the resolver rejects blocks the whole policy snapshot."
  ],
  "owners": [
    {
      "input": "corp.example",
      "role": "override",
      "swift": { "accept": true, "canonical": "corp.example" },
      "rust": { "accept": true, "canonical": "corp.example" }
    },
    {
      "input": "CORP.Example.",
      "role": "override",
      "swift": { "accept": true, "canonical": "corp.example" },
      "rust": { "accept": true, "canonical": "corp.example" }
    },
    {
      "input": "münchen.de",
